  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following recent Diwali celebrations, Delhi has faced sustained high levels of air pollution, with reports indicating it has surpassed Lahore as the world's most polluted city. Air quality monitoring stations throughout the capital are consistently reporting readings in the very poor to severe range, with some areas documenting an Air Quality Index (AQI) as high as 494. Factors identified by experts as driving these elevated pollution levels include vehicle emissions and seasonal biomass burning. While light rain is anticipated, there is skepticism regarding its potential to provide a significant reduction in the hazardous smog. Local authorities and monitoring bodies continue to track the data across 54 stations, as concern grows over the health implications for the city's residents. Similar concerns regarding air quality management have also been noted in other urban centers like Kochi, where additional monitoring infrastructure is being planned.",
